WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.200
-Welcome, welcome,
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.734
You're here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:09.701
I appreciate it, guys.
Tomorrow is Halloween.

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:11.701
Yeah.

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:14.033
I read that this year some
of the most popular costumes

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:18.067
are Barbie, Spider-Man,
and Wednesday Addams,

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:21.701
while the least popular costume
is once again Sexy Ron DeSantis.

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:23.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:25.334
Well, tomorrow New York City
will close down

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:27.567
a bunch of streets
for trick or treating.

00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:29.634
Yep, they'll have candy,
decorations,

00:00:29.634 --> 00:00:32.334
and maybe even a surprise visit
from "Doughnut Rat".

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:34.234
-Introducing "Doughnut Rat".

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:37.334
Viral video showing the rat
dragging a glazed donut

00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:40.400
along the subway tracks
of a lower Manhattan station.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.334
And check it out --
the rat even shares the treat

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:43.701
with his friend.

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:45.300
-Oh, my gosh. Yeah.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.767
Halloween is almost here,
and tonight at the White House,

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:50.968
the Bidens hosted
trick or treaters.

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:52.334
Yeah, things got off
to a rough start

00:00:52.334 --> 00:00:54.334
when Biden told the kid,
"Nice zombie costume."

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:56.033
The kid was like, "I'm you."

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:58.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:01.033
[ Applause ]

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:02.801
[ Cheering ]

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:04.534
"Get out of here!"

00:01:04.534 --> 00:01:06.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:06.634 --> 00:01:08.667
I don't think Biden's
quite up with the times.

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:10.300
Whenever he saw
a Taylor Swift costume,

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:13.234
he was like, "Greta Garbo?

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:15.634
Jean Harlow?"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:17.434
But it was adorable
when Biden asked kids,

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:18.567
"Who are you supposed to be?"

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:20.100
And a little less adorable
when he asked,

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.367
"And who am I again?"

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:23.968
But it was --
But it was nice

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:25.367
watching Biden hand out candy,

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:26.934
except when he reached
into the wrong pocket

00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:28.334
and gave out a Flomax pill.

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:29.467
It's like, no, that's --

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:30.734
"You'll thank me
when you're older.

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:32.100
You'll thank me..."

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.334
So more political news.

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:35.968
Over the weekend,
Mike pence officially suspended

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:38.701
his 2024 presidential campaign.

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:41.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:44.634
Which raises
an interesting question.

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:46.868
Can you stop something
that never started?

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:49.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:51.901
Hey, I saw that yesterday
former President Trump

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:54.601
held a campaign rally
in Sioux City, Iowa,

00:01:54.601 --> 00:01:56.534
but he didn't seem to quite know
where he was.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:57.534
Watch this.

00:01:57.534 --> 00:01:59.000
-Well, thank you very much.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.167
And a very big hello to a place
where we've done very well.

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:04.434
Sioux Falls. Thank you
very much, Sioux Falls.

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:05.434
[ Crowd boos ]

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.400
So Sioux City, let me ask you...

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:18.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:21.234
"Wh-- Where was I?
Sioux city. Sioux city."

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:23.133
[ Laughs ]

00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:25.100
Biden was like, "Someone
help that poor old man.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:27.868
He's confused
and disoriented."

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:29.367
Even the biggest
Trump supporters are thinking,

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:31.133
"Maybe those gag orders
are a good idea."

00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:33.467
Yeah, it makes sense
that he was confused.

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:35.434
It was the first time in months
he's been in a room

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:37.501
without a jury, so, yeah.

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:40.267
[ Audience oohs, laughs ]

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:41.767
-Joke?
-Yeah.

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:43.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.467 --> 00:02:45.100
Then Trump was like,
"And I love your founder,

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.767
the great Dr. Sue."

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:48.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.501
"'Green Eggs and Ham',
the Grinch.

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:51.601
I love the Grinch."

00:02:51.601 --> 00:02:52.601
You guys hear about this?

00:02:52.601 --> 00:02:53.734
During a trip to China,

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:55.334
California Governor Gavin Newsom

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:57.801
played a basketball game
with some school kids.

00:02:57.801 --> 00:02:59.501
Let's see how that went.

00:02:59.501 --> 00:03:02.567
[ Indistinct chatter ]

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.100
Ooh, good spin. Yeah.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.567
Hi-yah!
[ Audience oohs ]

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:09.067
[ Laughs ]

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:13.100
Yeah.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:15.968
Yeah, not every day that you see
a governor

00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:18.100
pick up a technical foul
against a 7 year old.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:19.400
It's like...

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.067
[ Grunts ]

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:24.567
Oh, have you guys heard
about this Toyota recall?

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:26.834
Toyota? It's not good.
Check -- Check this out.

00:03:26.834 --> 00:03:28.601
-A recall alert
for you this morning.

00:03:28.601 --> 00:03:32.767
Toyota recalling
more than 750,000 SUVs.

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:35.968
Toyota says the SUVs have an
issue in the front lower bumper

00:03:35.968 --> 00:03:39.868
that can cause the mounting tabs
to detach and fall off.

00:03:39.868 --> 00:03:44.167
-What?
Oh, man. I drive a Toyota.

00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:45.434
-Geez. Sorry, Tariq.

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:48.167
-I mean, it's not a big deal.
I mean, it's okay.

00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:51.901
I still have my trusty
Honda Civic Hatchback.

00:03:51.901 --> 00:03:54.567
-Oh.
-"Oh", what, Jimmy?

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.901
-Roll the clip.
-Honda is recalling more than

00:03:56.901 --> 00:04:02.934
176,000 2022 to '24 Civic sedans
and hatchbacks.

00:04:02.934 --> 00:04:04.934
-What?!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.934 --> 00:04:06.501
-You don't have another way
to get around?

00:04:06.501 --> 00:04:08.868
-I mean, I guess I could borrow
my friend's Tesla.

00:04:08.868 --> 00:04:11.400
-A recall alert --
Tesla is recalling

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.968
tens of thousands
of its newer vehicles.

00:04:13.968 --> 00:04:16.334
-Oh, come on.
-Yeah. I'm sorry, Tariq.

00:04:16.334 --> 00:04:18.100
-Now, how am I supposed
to get to the store?

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.934
I still need to buy candy
for trick or treat tomorrow.

00:04:20.934 --> 00:04:22.701
-You don't have anything
lying around the house?

00:04:22.701 --> 00:04:24.834
-I could check
my kitten -- kitchen.

00:04:24.834 --> 00:04:27.033
Excuse me, but all I have

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:29.567
is Best Buy Insignia
electric pressure cooker.

00:04:29.567 --> 00:04:31.767
-Check your kitten -- kitchen's,
excuse me.

00:04:31.767 --> 00:04:33.667
Best Buy says
that they are recalling

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:37.501
nearly a million Insignia
electric pressure cookers.

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:39.901
-Oh, come on.

00:04:39.901 --> 00:04:42.467
-I'm s-- Tough luck.
Do you have anything else?

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:44.601
-I mean, I just bought
a brand-new

00:04:44.601 --> 00:04:47.834
fyoot -- fruit purée pouches.

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:49.534
-The US Food and Drug
Administration is warning

00:04:49.534 --> 00:04:52.767
not to buy a brand of fyoot --
fruit purée pouches.

00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:56.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.033 --> 00:04:57.434
-What else do I even have?

00:04:57.434 --> 00:04:59.801
Just lots of diced
yellow onions --

00:04:59.801 --> 00:05:03.501
3 pound bags
and 8-ounce cumps -- cups.

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:05.400
-The recall alert
you need to know about.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:08.067
-It covers some lots
of diced yellow onions --

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:11.501
3-pound bags
and 8-ounce cumps -- cups.

00:05:11.501 --> 00:05:13.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.434 --> 00:05:15.400
-You know what? Fine!

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.534
-I'll just start handing out
my kids' old toys.

00:05:17.534 --> 00:05:19.901
I mean, he can have
some Thomas &amp; Friends --

00:05:19.901 --> 00:05:22.968
you know, Wooden Rail --
Ray-uh Rail --

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:25.434
Troublesome Trucks and Crates.

00:05:25.434 --> 00:05:26.934
[ Laughter ]
[ Cymbal crash ]

00:05:26.934 --> 00:05:28.934
-The recall involves
roughly 21,000

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:32.634
of the Thomas &amp; Friends
Wooden Rail-ray -- Railway

00:05:32.634 --> 00:05:34.667
Troublesome Trucks and Crates.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.868 --> 00:05:40.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:40.267 --> 00:05:41.934
-That's a lot.
Can you believe this?

00:05:41.934 --> 00:05:44.634
-Don't -- Don't encourage me.

00:05:44.634 --> 00:05:47.701
-Do you believe this?
This is terrible.

00:05:47.701 --> 00:05:49.868
-That's it, man!
-I'm sure there's something

00:05:49.868 --> 00:05:51.901
that you can give
to trick-or-treaters.

00:05:51.901 --> 00:05:53.934
-What do I even have left?
Dog food?!

00:05:53.934 --> 00:05:55.501
-Well, what kind
of dog food is it?

00:05:55.501 --> 00:05:57.534
-Well, it's TFP Nutrition's

00:05:57.534 --> 00:05:59.567
Retriever All Life Stages

00:05:59.567 --> 00:06:04.701
Mini Chunk Micro Chicken Recipe
Dry Dog Food.

00:06:04.701 --> 00:06:06.033
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.033 --> 00:06:08.434
-My goodness. That is a title.

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:10.801
-The FDA is recalling
TFP Nutrition's

00:06:10.801 --> 00:06:13.000
Retriever All Life Stages

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:16.033
Mini Chunk Chicken Recipe
Dry Dog Food.

00:06:16.033 --> 00:06:17.567
My goodness. That is a title.

00:06:17.567 --> 00:06:20.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.367
-I'm done.

00:06:21.367 --> 00:06:23.234
-Tariq Trotter, everybody.
Tariq Trotter.

00:06:23.234 --> 00:06:24.901
-That's...

00:06:24.901 --> 00:06:26.033
♪♪

00:06:26.033 --> 00:06:27.834
That's a lot of stuff
to go through.

00:06:27.834 --> 00:06:30.234
[ Applause ]

00:06:30.234 --> 00:06:32.334
-I feel bad for him.
-He had a tough night. Yeah.

00:06:32.334 --> 00:06:34.868
-Oh, man.
-I got some movie news.

00:06:34.868 --> 00:06:36.801
This weekend,
"Five Nights at Freddy's"

00:06:36.801 --> 00:06:40.300
won the box office,
bringing in $130 million.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:42.801
-Ooh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:42.801 --> 00:06:45.133
-It was so huge that they're
already planning a sequel,

00:06:45.133 --> 00:06:46.567
and it looks even scarier.

00:06:46.567 --> 00:06:48.501
Check this out.

00:06:48.501 --> 00:06:51.434
-They survived
"Five Nights at Freddy's,"

00:06:51.434 --> 00:06:55.167
but this time
they're pushed to the edge.

00:06:55.167 --> 00:06:57.100
Their sanity is tested.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:00.801
And no one will escape.

00:07:00.801 --> 00:07:02.267
Next fall, it's...

00:07:02.267 --> 00:07:05.667
"Six Hours on Spirit Airlines."

00:07:05.667 --> 00:07:06.734
[ Cabin bell dings ]

00:07:08.267 --> 00:07:10.033
-[ Screams ]

00:07:10.033 --> 00:07:12.267
-Only supposed to be 45 minutes.

00:07:12.267 --> 00:07:14.734
"Six hours?
Let me off this thing."

00:07:14.734 --> 00:07:17.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:17.133 --> 00:07:19.033
Finally, speaking of
Spirit Airlines,

00:07:19.033 --> 00:07:21.167
they just announced that
they're suspending training

00:07:21.167 --> 00:07:25.734
for new pilots and flight
attendants until further notice.

00:07:25.734 --> 00:07:28.434
I get if you have to do that,
but why announce it?

00:07:28.434 --> 00:07:29.968
We have a great show.

00:07:29.968 --> 00:07:32.000
Give it up for the Roots,
everybody. Come on, now.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.701
-♪ She wanna know
if we can be together ♪

00:07:33.701 --> 00:07:35.801
♪ Even if it ain't
gonna be forever ♪

00:07:35.801 --> 00:07:37.200
♪ It can only be for one night ♪

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:39.601
♪ The only thing I ever loved
in my life was the mic ♪

00:07:39.601 --> 00:07:42.868
♪ Uh-huh, come on ♪

00:07:42.868 --> 00:07:46.133
-Whoo!

00:07:46.133 --> 00:07:48.267
What a show we have
for you tonight.

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:51.267
He's currently starring
in the play "Waiting for Godot"

00:07:51.267 --> 00:07:54.167
at the Polonsky Shakespeare
Theater in Brooklyn.

00:07:54.167 --> 00:07:56.534
Michael Shannon is here tonight!

00:07:56.534 --> 00:07:59.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:03.067
Some very talented people here
tonight.

00:08:03.067 --> 00:08:04.567
She is a Tony winner

00:08:04.567 --> 00:08:07.300
who you can see in
"Sweeney Todd" on Broadway.

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:09.501
Annaleigh Ashford is joining us.

00:08:09.501 --> 00:08:10.734
-So funny.

00:08:10.734 --> 00:08:11.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:11.767 --> 00:08:14.334
Mind-blowing.
-Did you see --

00:08:14.334 --> 00:08:15.934
-I would put that performance

00:08:15.934 --> 00:08:17.434
up with a Nathan Lane
or a Martin short.

00:08:17.434 --> 00:08:19.300
That funny. Unbelievable.

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:21.133
-She was like
Lucille Ball funny.

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:22.701
-Crazy.
-When she goes down the stairs.

00:08:22.701 --> 00:08:23.934
-Down the stairs? Oh, my God.

00:08:23.934 --> 00:08:25.934
-That's the funniest thing ever.
-Got to go see it.

00:08:25.934 --> 00:08:27.901
-Speaking of funny...
-Who?

00:08:27.901 --> 00:08:30.267
-Jesus Trejo is here!

00:08:30.267 --> 00:08:33.167
Very funny comedian.
[ Chuckles ]

00:08:33.167 --> 00:08:35.000
"Practicing?"

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:37.300
That's his new special
on YouTube.

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:39.534
Well, guys, it's Monday night,
and you know what that means.

00:08:39.534 --> 00:08:41.534
It's "Tonight Show"
Trivia Night.

00:08:41.534 --> 00:08:43.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:43.968 --> 00:08:47.334
-♪ "Tonight Show" Trivia Night ♪

00:08:47.334 --> 00:08:48.934
-Yeah. Fun. I love trivia.

00:08:48.934 --> 00:08:50.300
Higgins, you want to explain
how this works?

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:52.133
-I would love to.
Yes, Jimmy,

00:08:52.133 --> 00:08:54.567
to test your knowledge
on a wide variety of topics,

00:08:54.567 --> 00:08:57.033
I'm going to be asking you
a series of trivia questions,

00:08:57.033 --> 00:09:00.267
and all you have to do
is answer them correctly.

00:09:00.267 --> 00:09:02.067
-Alright. This is easy.
I love trivia. Let's do this.

00:09:02.067 --> 00:09:03.467
-Ready? First question.

00:09:06.834 --> 00:09:08.501
-Um, Fort Knox.
[ Buzzer ]

00:09:08.501 --> 00:09:11.634
-Ooh, close.
The deodorant aisle at CVS.

00:09:11.634 --> 00:09:13.400
[ Laughter ]

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:16.100
So close, so close.
Okay. Ready?

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:21.734
-Easy. Rice Krispies.
[ Buzzer ]

00:09:21.734 --> 00:09:23.234
-Oh, no. Incorrect.

00:09:23.234 --> 00:09:25.400
Joe Biden when he stands up.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:27.868
Almost. You almost got it.
Almost got it.

00:09:27.868 --> 00:09:29.968
Alright, Jimmy, ready?
-Yep.

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:36.234
-"What is the meaning of life?"

00:09:36.234 --> 00:09:37.701
[ Buzzer ]
-Judges?

00:09:37.701 --> 00:09:40.367
No. "Why is pickleball
so popular?"

00:09:40.367 --> 00:09:42.501
[ Laughter ]
For centuries!

00:09:42.501 --> 00:09:44.133
-I don't know why.
-For hundreds of years,

00:09:44.133 --> 00:09:45.534
they've been trying
to answer that.

00:09:45.534 --> 00:09:47.801
Alright, Jimmy,
you'll get this one.

00:09:51.934 --> 00:09:54.267
-X.
[ Buzzer ]

00:09:54.267 --> 00:09:56.934
-Wrong. Twitter.
They call it Twitter.

00:09:56.934 --> 00:09:58.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:58.501 --> 00:10:00.267
-Ah, yeah.
-Close. You almost got it.

00:10:00.267 --> 00:10:01.901
You almost got it.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:10:01.901 --> 00:10:03.467
Okay. Ready?
You're going to get this one.

00:10:03.467 --> 00:10:04.801
I know.
-Mm-hmm.

00:10:04.801 --> 00:10:08.234
-What's the most common place
for senior citizens --

00:10:08.234 --> 00:10:10.934
for senior citizens --
where do they go

00:10:10.934 --> 00:10:13.901
to enjoy their golden years?
Senior citizens.

00:10:13.901 --> 00:10:15.567
Where do they go?
-Florida.

00:10:15.567 --> 00:10:16.968
[ Buzzer ]

00:10:16.968 --> 00:10:19.701
-No. Congress. Congress.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:19.701 --> 00:10:21.667
-"Preach!"
-Preach.

00:10:21.667 --> 00:10:23.367
-Preach.
-Preach.

00:10:23.367 --> 00:10:27.000
-That was my political --
That's from my stand-up act.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:28.701
-Your stand-up act, by the way.
Yeah, I got to make it.

00:10:28.701 --> 00:10:31.267
-You got to go see it.
I take a newspaper, I just riff.

00:10:31.267 --> 00:10:33.400
-No, I'm busy.
-Oh, really, what are you doing?

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:35.000
-Very busy.
-What about tomorrow?

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:36.801
-That's Halloween.
-Oh.

00:10:36.801 --> 00:10:38.467
